description:
Source: KB review 2026-11-04 (P3).

**Today:** `data/kb` holds text and chunks only. Every machine re-embeds about 5M tokens through the gateway, which needs an OpenAI key and LiteLLM (est. 5-10 min, ~0.10 USD) before the first search. A from-scratch crawl takes 1.7 h or more, but the snapshot already avoids that.

**Design (cleaner option from the review):**

* `export-snapshot --with-vectors` writes the vectors next to the chunks;
* the manifest records `embedding: {model, dim}`;
* `import-snapshot` loads the vectors when the model matches, refuses when it doesn't, and still applies the leak guard;
* the large file stays out of git and is shared via a drive, while the text-only snapshot stays in git.

**Acceptance:**

* importing on a machine with no gateway gives a working `kb_search` (the query embedding still needs the gateway; say so);
* import time is measured;
* the leak-guard tests still pass.
